
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:set@

%9Parameters:%9

    -clear:      Removes the setting's value from the configuration.
    -default:    Restore the setting to its default value.
    -section:    Print settings under the specified section

    The setting and the value; if no value is given, the list of settings that
    matched will be returned. If no arguments are given, all the settings will
    be displayed.

%9Description:%9

    Modifies the value of a setting; boolean settings accept only ON, OFF and
    TOGGLE.

    Please remember that you need to use the SAVE command to store the changes
    into your configuration.

    The value of a secret is not shown: settings with password, passwd,
    secret or token in the name, names ending in api_key and the names
    listed in hidden_settings (space or comma separated, empty by default)
    print as '(secret, set - not shown)', and tab completion does not put
    their value on the input line, so it stays off the screen, the
    window's log and connected web clients. Scripts and $variables still
    get the real value; an empty setting prints as empty.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET
    /SET nick mike
    /SET -clear nick
    /SET log_timestamp %%H:%%H:%%S
    /SET -default log_timestamp
    /SET -section lookandfeel
    /SET close

%9See also:%9 SAVE, TOGGLE

